Source: Android Kotlin Style > Source files > Naming

### Naming

If a source file contains only a single top-level class, the file name
should reflect the case-sensitive name plus the `.kt` extension. Otherwise,
if a source file contains multiple top-level declarations, choose a name
that describes the contents of the file, apply PascalCase (camelCase is
acceptable if the filename is plural), and append the `.kt` extension.

// MyClass.kt class MyClass { }

// Bar.kt class Bar { } fun Runnable.toBar(): Bar = Bar()

// Map.kt fun <T, O> Set<T>.map(func: (T) -> O): List<O> = emptyList() fun <T, O> List<T>.map(func: (T) -> O): List<O> = emptyList()

// extensions.kt fun MyClass.process() = { /* ... */ } fun MyResult.print() = { /* ... */ }

