Source: Android Kotlin Style > Source files > Formatting > Documentation > Formatting

#### Formatting

The basic formatting of KDoc blocks is seen in this example:

/** * Multiple lines of KDoc text are written here, * wrapped normally… */ fun method(arg: String) { // … }

...or in this single-line example:

/** An especially short bit of KDoc. */

The basic form is always acceptable. The single-line form may be
substituted when the entirety of the KDoc block (including comment markers)
can fit on a single line. Note that this only applies when there are no
block tags such as `@return`.

