Source: Cpp Core Guidelines > <a name="s-philosophy"></a>P: Philosophy > <a name="rp-direct"></a>P.1: Express ideas directly in code > <a name="rp-leak"></a>P.8: Don't leak any resources > Reason > Example, bad

##### Example, bad

 void f(const char* name)
 {
 FILE* input = fopen(name, "r");
 // ...
 if (something) return; // bad: if something == true, a file handle is leaked
 // ...
 fclose(input);
 }

Prefer [RAII](#rr-raii):

 void f(const char* name)
 {
 ifstream input {name};
 // ...
 if (something) return; // OK: no leak
 // ...
 }

**See also**: [The resource management section](#s-resource)

