Source: Cpp Core Guidelines > <a name="s-functions"></a>F: Functions > <a name="ss-fct-def"></a>F.def: Function definitions > <a name="rf-package"></a>F.1: "Package" meaningful operations as carefully named functions > Reason > Example

##### Example

 sort(a, b, [](T x, T y) { return x.rank() < y.rank() && x.value() < y.value(); });

Naming that lambda breaks up the expression into its logical parts and provides a strong hint to the meaning of the lambda.

 auto lessT = [](T x, T y) { return x.rank() < y.rank() && x.value() < y.value(); };

 sort(a, b, lessT);

The shortest code is not always the best for performance or maintainability.

