Source: Cpp Core Guidelines > <a name="s-functions"></a>F: Functions > <a name="ss-call"></a>F.call: Parameter passing > <a name="rf-range"></a>F.24: Use a `span<T>` or a `span_p<T>` to designate a half-open sequence > Reason > Example

##### Example

A `span` represents a range of elements, but how do we manipulate elements of that range?

 void f(span<int> s)
 {
 // range traversal (guaranteed correct)
 for (int x : s) cout << x << '\n';

 // C-style traversal (potentially checked)
 for (gsl::index i = 0; i < s.size(); ++i) cout << s[i] << '\n';

 // random access (potentially checked)
 s[7] = 9;

 // extract pointers (potentially checked)
 std::sort(&s[0], &s[s.size() / 2]);
 }

