Source: Cpp Core Guidelines > <a name="s-functions"></a>F: Functions > <a name="ss-call"></a>F.call: Parameter passing > <a name="rf-return-ptr"></a>F.42: Return a `T*` to indicate a position (only) > Reason > Example

##### Example

 Node* find(Node* t, const string& s) // find s in a binary tree of Nodes
 {
 if (!t || t->name == s) return t;
 if ((auto p = find(t->left, s))) return p;
 if ((auto p = find(t->right, s))) return p;
 return nullptr;
 }

If it isn't the `nullptr`, the pointer returned by `find` indicates a `Node` holding `s`.
Importantly, that does not imply a transfer of ownership of the pointed-to object to the caller.

