Source: Cpp Core Guidelines > <a name="s-class"></a>C: Classes and class hierarchies > <a name="ss-dtor"></a>C.dtor: Destructors > <a name="rc-dtor-release"></a>C.31: All resources acquired by a class must be released by the class's destructor > Reason > Note

##### Note

A class can hold pointers and references to objects that it does not own.
Obviously, such objects should not be `delete`d by the class's destructor.
For example:

 Preprocessor pp { /* ... */ };
 Parser p { pp, /* ... */ };
 Type_checker tc { p, /* ... */ };

Here `p` refers to `pp` but does not own it.

