##### Alternative

Wrap a `union` in a class together with a type field.

The C++17 `variant` type (found in `<variant>`) does that for you:

 variant<int, double> v;
 v = 123; // v holds an int
 int x = get<int>(v);
 v = 123.456; // v holds a double
 double w = get<double>(v);

