Source: Cpp Core Guidelines > <a name="s-enum"></a>Enum: Enumerations > <a name="renum-macro"></a>Enum.1: Prefer enumerations over macros > Reason > Example

##### Example

First some bad old code:

 // webcolors.h (third party header)
 #define RED 0xFF0000
 #define GREEN 0x00FF00
 #define BLUE 0x0000FF

 // productinfo.h
 // The following define product subtypes based on color
 #define RED 0
 #define PURPLE 1
 #define BLUE 2

 int webby = BLUE; // webby == 2; probably not what was desired

Instead use an `enum`:

 enum class Web_color { red = 0xFF0000, green = 0x00FF00, blue = 0x0000FF };
 enum class Product_info { red = 0, purple = 1, blue = 2 };

 int webby = blue; // error: be specific
 Web_color webby = Web_color::blue;

We used an `enum class` to avoid name clashes.

