Source: Cpp Core Guidelines > <a name="s-enum"></a>Enum: Enumerations > <a name="renum-macro"></a>Enum.1: Prefer enumerations over macros > <a name="renum-oper"></a>Enum.4: Define operations on enumerations for safe and simple use > Reason > Example

##### Example

 enum class Day { mon, tue, wed, thu, fri, sat, sun };

 Day& operator++(Day& d)
 {
 return d = (d == Day::sun) ? Day::mon : static_cast<Day>(static_cast<int>(d)+1);
 }

 Day today = Day::sat;
 Day tomorrow = ++today;

The use of a `static_cast` is not pretty, but

 Day& operator++(Day& d)
 {
 return d = (d == Day::sun) ? Day::mon : Day{++d}; // error
 }

is an infinite recursion, and writing it without a cast, using a `switch` on all cases is long-winded.

