Source: Cpp Core Guidelines > <a name="s-resource"></a>R: Resource management > <a name="rr-raii"></a>R.1: Manage resources automatically using resource handles and RAII (Resource Acquisition Is Initialization) > <a name="rr-ptr"></a>R.3: A raw pointer (a `T*`) is non-owning > Reason > Example

##### Example

 template<typename T>
 class X {
 public:
 T* p; // bad: it is unclear whether p is owning or not
 T* q; // bad: it is unclear whether q is owning or not
 // ...
 };

We can fix that problem by making ownership explicit:

 template<typename T>
 class X2 {
 public:
 owner<T*> p; // OK: p is owning
 T* q; // OK: q is not owning
 // ...
 };

