Source: Cpp Core Guidelines > <a name="s-expr"></a>ES: Expressions and statements > ES.dcl: Declarations > <a name="res-name-length"></a>ES.7: Keep common and local names short, and keep uncommon and non-local names longer > Reason > Example

##### Example

Unconventional and short non-local names obscure code:

 void use1(const string& s)
 {
 // ...
 tt(s); // bad: what is tt()?
 // ...
 }

Better, give non-local entities readable names:

 void use1(const string& s)
 {
 // ...
 trim_tail(s); // better
 // ...
 }

Here, there is a chance that the reader knows what `trim_tail` means and that the reader can remember it after looking it up.

