Source: Cpp Core Guidelines > <a name="s-expr"></a>ES: Expressions and statements > ES.dcl: Declarations > <a name="res-reuse"></a>ES.12: Do not reuse names in nested scopes > Reason > Example, bad

##### Example, bad

 int d = 0;
 // ...
 if (cond) {
 // ...
 d = 9;
 // ...
 }
 else {
 // ...
 int d = 7;
 // ...
 d = value_to_be_returned;
 // ...
 }

 return d;

If this is a large `if`-statement, it is easy to overlook that a new `d` has been introduced in the inner scope.
This is a known source of bugs.
Sometimes such reuse of a name in an inner scope is called "shadowing".

