##### Example

 void use(int arg)
 {
 int i; // bad: uninitialized variable
 // ...
 i = 7; // initialize i
 }

No, `i = 7` does not initialize `i`; it assigns to it. Also, `i` can be read in the `...` part. Better:

 void use(int arg) // OK
 {
 int i = 7; // OK: initialized
 string s; // OK: default initialized
 // ...
 }

