Source: Cpp Core Guidelines > <a name="s-expr"></a>ES: Expressions and statements > <a name="ss-numbers"></a>Arithmetic > <a name="res-nonnegative"></a>ES.106: Don't try to avoid negative values by using `unsigned` > Reason > Alternatives

##### Alternatives

* use signed integers and check for `x >= 0`
* use a positive integer type
* use an integer subrange type
* `Assert(-1 < x)`

For example

 struct Positive {
 int val;
 Positive(int x) :val{x} { Assert(0 < x); }
 operator int() { return val; }
 };

 int f(Positive arg) { return arg; }

 int r1 = f(2);
 int r2 = f(-2); // throws

