Source: Cpp Core Guidelines > <a name="s-templates"></a>T: Templates and generic programming > <a name="ss-temp-other"></a>Other template rules > <a name="rt-check-class"></a>T.150: Check that a class matches a concept using `static_assert` > Reason > Example

##### Example

 class X {
 public:
 X() = delete;
 X(const X&) = default;
 X(X&&) = default;
 X& operator=(const X&) = default;
 // ...
 };

Somewhere, possibly in an implementation file, let the compiler check the desired properties of `X`:

 static_assert(Default_constructible<X>); // error: X has no default constructor
 static_assert(Copyable<X>); // error: we forgot to define X's move constructor

