Source: Cpp Core Guidelines > <a name="s-stdlib"></a>SL: The Standard Library > <a name="ss-io"></a>SL.io: Iostream > <a name="rio-low"></a>SL.io.1: Use character-level input only when you have to > Reason > Example

##### Example

 char c;
 char buf[128];
 int i = 0;
 while (cin.get(c) && !isspace(c) && i < 128)
 buf[i++] = c;
 if (i == 128) {
 // ... handle too long string ....
 }

Better (much simpler and probably faster):

 string s;
 s.reserve(128);
 cin >> s;

and the `reserve(128)` is probably not worthwhile.

