use of '= default'.

```c++
struct A {
 A() : i(5), j(10.0) {}
 A(int i) : i(i), j(10.0) {}
 int i;
 double j;
};

// becomes

struct A {
 A() {}
 A(int i) : i(i) {}
 int i{5};
 double j{10.0};
};
```

**Note:**
Only converts member initializers for built-in types, enums, and pointers.
The `readability-redundant-member-init` check will remove redundant member
initializers for classes.

